  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "How you travel: (으)로",
     "texto": [
      "A means of transport takes **로** (after a vowel or ㄹ) or **으로** (after another consonant): 버스**로** (by bus), 지하철**로** (by subway), 택시**로** (by taxi), 기차**로** (by train), 비행기**로** (by plane).",
      "On foot is **걸어서**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Getting on, getting off, changing",
     "texto": [
      "**타요** = to get on, to take. It takes 을/를: 버스**를** 타요 (I take the bus).",
      "**내려요** = to get off: 서울역**에서** 내려요 (I get off at Seoul station).",
      "**갈아타요** = to change (transport)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "From… to… and how long it takes",
     "texto": [
      "Between two places: **에서** (from) … **까지** (to). 집**에서** 회사**까지** = from home to the company.",
      "**얼마나 걸려요?** = How long does it take?",
      "Duration: minutes, as always (삼십 분). Hours of duration are **시간**, with native Korean numbers: 한 **시간** (one hour), 두 **시간** (two hours). Do not confuse it with 시, which is the hour on the clock.",
      "**시간** also means «time»: **시간이 없어요** = I don't have time."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
